## Context

- **No pending analyst tasks at start of run.** Proactively advanced to Phase 3 sub-phenotype analysis.
- **Phase 3 complete on MIMIC-IV demo.** FP sub-phenotype analysis: signal (developed sepsis, n=16) vs noise (didn't, n=11) at 80% specificity.
- **Key finding: Age paradox.** All FPs older than TNs (d=+0.86, Phase 2), but signal FPs younger than noise FPs (d=-2.00, p<0.0001). Two-population model:
  - "Chronic illness" FPs (noise): older, stable renal/anemia, don't progress.
  - "Pre-clinical" FPs (signal): younger, acute coagulopathy (PTT d=+1.55, p=0.002) + renal dysfunction (creatinine d=+0.84, p=0.030).
- **Attenuated TP hypothesis partially supported.** 59% features same direction, 30% attenuated. BUN (ratio=0.64) and creatinine (ratio=0.58) support model. Age amplified (ratio=2.57), consistent with FPs being a distinct older population.
- **Clustering weak** (silhouette=0.220, Fisher p=0.624) — unsupervised separation doesn't align cleanly with outcomes at n=27.
- **Pre-clinical signature candidates:** PTT (coagulopathy), creatinine, BUN (renal), age (paradoxical).
- **Outputs:** data/results/false-positive-biomarker-mining/phase3/ (10 files). Script: scripts/run_fp_subphenotype_analysis.py. Journal entry id=14.
- **Tasks created:** research_director task #21 (review Phase 3 findings, novel-finding), developer task #22 (add stratified IRR to full MIMIC-IV pipeline).
- **Existing tasks:** developer #13 (full MIMIC-IV adapter, pending), research_director #12 (review Phase 2, pending).
- **Next:** (1) Full MIMIC-IV for adequate power. (2) Stratified IRR by sub-type. (3) Signal/noise FP classifier. (4) Cross-domain FP comparison (CRC data available in data/diagnostics/crc-liquid-biopsy-panel/).
